<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <title>Dynasty Tools</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <header class="site">
    <h1>Dynasty Tools</h1>
    <div class="tagline">Best-ball projections and analytics for Sleeper dynasty leagues.</div>
    <nav>
      <a href="https://github.com/stephenmsoward-cmd/Stephen-dynasty-football-assistant">GitHub</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <h2>Leagues</h2>
  <ul class="league-list">
    {% for r in reports %}
    <li>
      <a href="leagues/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ r.name }}</a>
      <div class="meta">
        {{ r.season }} season &middot; {{ r.total_rosters }} teams &middot; {{ r.ppr }} PPR
      </div>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <div class="methodology">
    <h3>What this is</h3>
    <p>
      For each team in a Sleeper dynasty league, this site computes the
      <strong>optimal starting lineup</strong> from all rostered players (excluding taxi and IR)
      using the league's actual slot configuration. Values come from FantasyCalc's dynasty
      trade values and reflect multi-year expected production with age baked in.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's a way to see how teams stack up if everyone fielded their best possible lineup
      each week — the "best ball" version of the standings.
    </p>
    <h3>Add your league</h3>
    <p>
      Open a pull request adding your league ID and a slug to
      <code>leagues.yml</code>. The nightly Action will build a report at
      <code>/leagues/&lt;slug&gt;/</code>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <footer class="site">
    Generated {{ generated_at }}.
  </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
